---
title: "G5 Hands: ft-camd, ft-hands, when tracking runs and parks, hand roles, near input, the hand ray and pinches (78e93b1, G5Hands.tla)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Off, stopped, or nothing held
    lg1: Running, tracking, or held, as it should be
    lg2: Between: parked, waiting out a grace or a hold, restarting
    lg3: Let go of or ended early: a pause, a timeout, someone else
    lg4: Suspected open bug: the state that breaks the rule
    lg5: H5-1 open, TrackerIdleInPause: a pause before hand tracking ever ran since login. The run folder is missing, so update_park writes no park file but remembers parked. Tracking that starts later in the pause (the desktop opened from the dashboard) tracks through the game (red H5-1.1-3, TLC FreshBoot, 3 steps, FreshBootFix holds)
    lg6: H5-2 open, minor, TrackerIdleInPause: hand interaction switched off during a pause. set_hands empties keep and unparks, and nothing stops the units the pause kept, so they track through the game. pause-test.py 262-263 expects the worker to stop them (red H5-2.1-2, TLC SwitchOff, 4 steps)
    lg7: H5-3 open, minor, TrackerIdleInPause: ft-cutouts' units aren't in the pause's UNITS, and without hand interaction nothing parks them, so the cutouts' tracker runs through VR games (red H5-3.1-2, TLC Cutouts, 4 steps)
    lg8: H5-4 open, minor, TrackerIdleInPause and ParkLifts: the helper says vrdash only on a change, or every 5 s in a game. A helper that goes with the dashboard open (SteamVR restart, crash) leaves the relay's copy open, and a new relay thinks it closed. Outside a game, a manual pause stays unparked, or parks under an open dashboard (red H5-4.1-4, TLC Steady 7 steps, Restarts 6, DashFix and RestartsFix hold)
    lg9: Holds at 78e93b1: TypeOK in all 11 configs. TrackerIdleInPause and ParkLifts in DashFix (64 states), FreshBootFix (91), NoHands (96), RestartsFix (164). ParkLifts in every config without relay restarts. ft-hands quiet 2.5 s ends a held pinch (ft-pointer.cpp 3649-3672), a park ends gestures as lost
    lg10: G1 L2 and L3 are drawn there: NoHandsL2 re-finds L2 here in 3 steps (a desktop starting mid-pause starts camd and hands). L3's root: frametop-camd and frametop-hands have no Requisite=steamvr, which game_pause.py 577 assumes, only the hand view has it
    lg11: Escape hatches: H5-1, open and close the dashboard (update_park runs again) or resume. H5-2, H5-3, ft-handsctl off, ft-cutouts off, or resume and pause again. H5-4, open and close the dashboard, or start a game (the helper resends every 5 s)
    lg12: Another group: arrows into it are where G5 touches it, drawn there, not here
  }
